<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Utrecht</h1><p class="st-meta">1854 CE – 1858 CE · capital Utrecht</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A tiny Boer republic on the Buffalo River, created on land obtained from the Zulu king Mpande.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1854 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> farmers obtained a strip of land along the Buffalo River on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a> border from King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mpande">Mpande</a> and founded the village of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-utrecht">Utrecht</a>, organising themselves as a small independent republic.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known beyond its simple <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volksraad">Volksraad</a> government and a population of a few hundred farming families, who depended on good relations with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/zulu-kingdom">Zulu Kingdom</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-utrecht">Utrecht</a> joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-lydenburg">Republic of Lydenburg</a> in 1858, and with it entered the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/south-african-republic">South African Republic</a> in 1860. The district's border with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/zulu-kingdom">Zululand</a> remained disputed, a grievance behind the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-zulu-war">Anglo-Zulu War</a> of 1879.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/republic-of-utrecht.jpg" alt="Republic of Utrecht" width="320" height="238"><figcaption>Image: Janek Szymanowski · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:9_2_447_0018-Utrecht_Town_Hall-KZN-s.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1854 CE – 1858 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Utrecht</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Dutch Reformed Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dutch</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/south-africa">South Africa</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Utrecht Republic</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1856&amp;focus=republic-of-utrecht" aria-label="Republic of Utrecht on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5476 3191 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Utrecht lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5796 3447L5808 3357"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5808 3357h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5796 3447h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5796 3447h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1856&amp;focus=republic-of-utrecht">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
